										><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="rt-col-md-12 rt-col-sm-12 rt-col-xs-12 even-grid-item tss-grid-item slide-item swiper-slide even-grid-item default-margin tss-img-circle"><div class="single-item-wrapper"><div class="tss-meta-info tss-left"><div class="profile-img-wrapper"><img alt="JALC student Omar Naser sitting in chair." class="rt-responsive-img" src="https://www.jalc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/naser_1.jpg" /></div><h3 class="author-name">Omar Naser</h3><h4 class="author-bio"><span class="author-designation">Biological Science Student - Carbondale</span></h4></div><div class="item-content-wrapper tss-right"><span class="tss-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><div class="item-content"><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">My absolute favorite part of being a student at JALC was the friendly environment the staff and professors made on campus.</span></p>
</div><div class="tss-card-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div><div class="rt-col-md-12 rt-col-sm-12 rt-col-xs-12 even-grid-item tss-grid-item slide-item swiper-slide even-grid-item default-margin tss-img-circle"><div class="single-item-wrapper"><div class="tss-meta-info tss-left"><div class="profile-img-wrapper"><img alt="Makayla Collins smiling with arms crossed wearing a JALC sweatshirt." class="rt-responsive-img" src="https://www.jalc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/collins.jpg" /></div><h3 class="author-name">Makayla Collins</h3><h4 class="author-bio"><span class="author-designation">Nursing Student - Marion</span></h4></div><div class="item-content-wrapper tss-right"><span class="tss-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><div class="item-content"><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Because of JALC, I have grown into a more confident student, leader, and future nurse who is excited to make a difference.</span></p>
</div><div class="tss-card-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div><div class="rt-col-md-12 rt-col-sm-12 rt-col-xs-12 even-grid-item tss-grid-item slide-item swiper-slide even-grid-item default-margin tss-img-circle"><div class="single-item-wrapper"><div class="tss-meta-info tss-left"><div class="profile-img-wrapper"><img alt="Jacie Nunley standing with her colorful backpack over her shoulder smiling for a picture wearing a pink sweater and white shirt with a ponytail in front of a blue decorated wall." class="rt-responsive-img" src="https://www.jalc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/nunley.jpg" /></div><h3 class="author-name">Jacie Nunley</h3><h4 class="author-bio"><span class="author-designation">Associate in Science Student - Mackinaw</span></h4></div><div class="item-content-wrapper tss-right"><span class="tss-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><div class="item-content"><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">The student organizations are the part of John A. that really boosted my confidence and made me get back into the swing of school.</span></p>
</div><div class="tss-card-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div><div class="rt-col-md-12 rt-col-sm-12 rt-col-xs-12 even-grid-item tss-grid-item slide-item swiper-slide even-grid-item default-margin tss-img-circle"><div class="single-item-wrapper"><div class="tss-meta-info tss-left"><div class="profile-img-wrapper"><img alt="Evan Giles in John A. Logan College Automotive shirt with arms crossed." class="rt-responsive-img" src="https://www.jalc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/giles_2.jpg" /></div><h3 class="author-name">Evan Giles</h3><h4 class="author-bio"><span class="author-designation">Automotive Technology Student - Du Quoin</span></h4></div><div class="item-content-wrapper tss-right"><span class="tss-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><div class="item-content"><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Because of John A. Logan College, I feel like I have more of a family.</span></p>
</div><div class="tss-card-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div><div class="rt-col-md-12 rt-col-sm-12 rt-col-xs-12 even-grid-item tss-grid-item slide-item swiper-slide even-grid-item default-margin tss-img-circle"><div class="single-item-wrapper"><div class="tss-meta-info tss-left"><div class="profile-img-wrapper"><img alt="JALC Student Chandler Phemister stands in the hallway smiling and holding his backpack." class="rt-responsive-img" src="https://www.jalc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Chandler2.png" /></div><h3 class="author-name">Chandler Phemister</h3><h4 class="author-bio"><span class="author-designation">Associate in Arts &amp; Associate in Science Student - Marion</span></h4></div><div class="item-content-wrapper tss-right"><span class="tss-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><div class="item-content"><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">JALC has an incredibly supportive community and provides students with many opportunities for personal and professional growth.</span></p>
</div><div class="tss-card-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div></div></div><div class="rt-loading-overlay"></div><div class="rt-loading rt-ball-clip-rotate"><div></div></div></div></div>
